Description: Don't wait on the sysfs firmware fallback for iwl-dbg-cfg.ini
 With IWLWIFI_SUPPORT_DEBUG_OVERRIDES (enabled by defconfig-iwlwifi-public),
 iwl_drv_start() requests the optional iwl-dbg-cfg.ini synchronously during
 probe. L4T kernels set CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK=y, so a missing
 file falls back to a sysfs request. At boot, udev is itself running the
 modprobe that is probing the device and can't answer that request until
 probe returns, so probe stalls for the full 60 s fallback timeout and Wi-Fi
 comes up a minute late. request_firmware_direct() never uses the fallback.
 After the change, firmware loads about 40 ms after the module does.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-25
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/iwl-dbg-cfg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/iwl-dbg-cfg.c
@@ -264,7 +264,14 @@
 		return;
 
 	/* TODO: maybe add a per-device file? */
-	err = firmware_request_nowarn(&fw, "iwl-dbg-cfg.ini", dev);
+	/*
+	 * Optional file, requested synchronously from probe: never use the
+	 * sysfs fallback. L4T kernels force it (FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK),
+	 * and when udev loads the driver at boot it can't answer the request
+	 * until probe returns, so a missing file stalled probe for the 60 s
+	 * fallback timeout.
+	 */
+	err = request_firmware_direct(&fw, "iwl-dbg-cfg.ini", dev);
 	if (err)
 		return;
 
